  greetings:
  - Long trip. Please make it quick.
  - Good evening, officer. Or is it morning here?
  - Everything should be in order.
  - I've been in that queue for three hours.
  - My cousin said this station is friendly.
  - Is the bar still open after this?
  - Don't look at me like that. I'm just tired.
  - Here. All of it.
  - First time on Kestrel. Is it always this cold?
  - They told me to talk to you.
  - I have a connecting shuttle. Please.
  - You look like you need a drink more than I do.
  - Same as last time, officer.
  - Mind the papers, they got wet.
  - I'm only passing through.
  - Work is work. Where do I go?
  crimes:
  - Armed robbery.
  - Smuggling, three counts.
  - Escaped from a labor camp.
  - Desertion.
  - Forgery of transit papers.
  - Sabotage at a fuel depot.
  - Fraud, Meridian Hub.
  - Assault on an officer.
  flawLines:
  - flaw: 1
    key: expires
    line: It ran out? They told me I had until the end of the cycle.
  - flaw: 1
    key: expires
    line: It's only a little late, officer. The queue for renewals is months long.
  - flaw: 2
    key: expires
    line: I've been meaning to renew it. The office has been shut for weeks.
  - flaw: 2
    key: expires
    line: It still looks like me, doesn't it?
  - flaw: 3
    key: name
    line: A clerk's mistake. Everybody spells it differently.
  - flaw: 3
    key: name
    line: That's my name. More or less. They rushed the form.
  - flaw: 4
    key: id
    line: The numbers? I never look at the numbers.
  - flaw: 4
    key: id
    line: They must have typed it wrong at the consulate.
  - flaw: 6
    key: issued
    line: The consulate gave me that. Who else would have?
  - flaw: 6
    key: issued
    line: I paid good money for that stamp. I mean, the fee.
  - flaw: 7
    key: cargo
    line: It's only for personal use. All of it.
  - flaw: 7
    key: cargo
    line: Yesterday that was perfectly legal, officer.
  - flaw: 8
    key: origin
    line: I only lived there. I've nothing to do with what's going on.
  - flaw: 8
    key: origin
    line: That's where I'm from. I can't change it.
  - flaw: 9
    key: route
    line: We didn't even leave the ship there. I feel fine.
  - flaw: 9
    key: route
    line: A short stop for fuel. Nobody was sick. Nobody I saw.
  - flaw: 11
    key: name
    line: There must be plenty of people with that name.
  - flaw: 11
    key: name
    line: You've got the wrong one. I get that a lot.
  standingWanted:
  - name: DOVAN PRYCE
    id: DP-7342-18
    order: 0
    note: Armed robbery, New Hadra
  letters:
  - title: A letter from home
    body: "Dad,\nThe heater rattles again, but it still works if you hit it twice.
      Mom hits it a lot.\nWe count the days. Don't work too hard.\n\u2014 Lena"
  - title: A letter from home
    body: "Dad,\nPip drew a picture of your station. It has too many windows and
      a cat on the roof.\nMom put it on the wall.\n\u2014 Lena"
  - title: A letter from home
    body: "Dad,\nPrices went up again at the depot. Everyone says it will get better
      after the winter.\nNobody says which winter.\n\u2014 Lena"
  - title: A letter from home
    body: "Dad,\nMom asks if you eat properly. I told her you do. Do you?\nWrite
      back when you can.\n\u2014 Lena"
  - title: A letter from home
    body: "Dad,\nThe neighbors left for the inner colonies last week. Their windows
      are dark now.\nPip waves at them anyway. We miss you.\n\u2014 Lena"
  - title: A letter from home
    body: "Dad,\nThere was a power cut all night. We sat under the blankets and Mom
      told stories about you.\nThey were mostly true.\n\u2014 Lena"
  - title: A letter from home
    body: "Dad,\nSchool wants new shoes for the winter term. Mom said we'll see.\nDon't
      worry about it. Just come home.\n\u2014 Lena"
  - title: A letter from home
    body: "Dad,\nI found your old jacket in the cupboard. It still smells like you,
      a little. I wear it to bed.\nHow long now?\n\u2014 Lena"
  - title: A letter from home
    body: "Dad,\nThe radio says the routes are getting worse. Mom says be careful
      who you let through.\nI say be careful who you don't.\n\u2014 Lena"
  - title: A letter from home
    body: "Dad,\nThe depot has started rationing soap. We smell like everybody else
      now, so nobody minds.\nWrite when you can.\n\u2014 Lena"
  - title: A letter from home
    body: "Dad,\nThe stairwell light has been out for a month. Pip and I count the
      steps now. Nineteen.\nCome home before we forget the number.\n\u2014 Lena"
  - title: A letter from home
    body: "Dad,\nSomebody painted over the old mural by the depot. You can still
      see the sun if you know where to look.\nWe know where to look.\n\u2014 Lena"
  - title: A letter from home
    body: "Dad,\nPip lost another tooth and wants to send it to you. Mom said the
      drone costs too much.\nIt is in a matchbox, waiting.\n\u2014 Lena"
  - title: A letter from home
    body: "Dad,\nThey moved the clinic to the other side of the river. It's a long
      walk. Mom says that's what legs are for.\nDon't worry.\n\u2014 Lena"
  - title: A letter from home
    body: "Dad,\nIt snowed indoors at school, right through the roof. We all thought
      it was wonderful.\nThe teachers did not.\n\u2014 Lena"
  - title: A letter from home
    body: "Dad,\nMom saw your name on an old list at the depot and stood there for
      a long time.\nShe didn't say anything. I just wanted you to know.\n\u2014 Lena"
  - title: A letter from home
    body: "Dad,\nThe neighbor's dog has decided it lives with us. We can't feed it.
      We feed it.\nPip named it Kestrel. How are the people up there?\n\u2014 Lena"
  - title: A letter from home
    body: "Dad,\nWe put your chair back at the table. It was in the way, but it looked
      wrong by the wall.\nSave what you can.\n\u2014 Lena"
  - title: A letter from home
    body: "Dad,\nThe radio played that song you hate. We all sang it, badly, on purpose.\nYou
      would have left the room.\n\u2014 Lena"
  - title: A letter from home
    body: "Dad,\nWe had soup three days in a row. Good soup, though. Mom says it
      counts as cooking.\nSave what you can. We can wait a bit longer.\n\u2014 Lena"
